### Synapse MinimalApi — Counter feature (value-type responses, cross-assembly RegisterGroup, CQRS enforcement)
###
### The Counter feature lives in a SEPARATE assembly (examples/MinimalApi.Counter). Its handlers and
### behaviors are wired through that assembly's own generated RegisterGroup, composed into this host via a
### second cfg.AddRegisterGroup(...). Every Counter message is IRequest<int> — a BARE value type — exercising
### the known-issue 001 path end-to-end:
###
###   • value-type (int) responses through the generated CLOSED CqrsBoundaryEnforcementBehavior<,int>
###   • a generated CLOSED open-generic [PipelineBehavior] (CounterTracingBehavior<,int>)
###   • CQRS boundary enforcement that rejects nested requests (illegal-nested endpoint)
###
### Run `dotnet run` in examples/MinimalApi, then execute requests top-to-bottom.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5225

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# 1. Query — current counter value (IRequest<int>)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### [Feature: value-type query, cross-assembly] Get the current counter value
### Expect: 200 OK, body is a bare int. Captures the value for the increment delta check below.
GET {{baseUrl}}/counter
Accept: application/json

> {%
    client.test("Get counter returns 200 with an int body", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "Expected 200 OK");
        client.assert(typeof response.body === "number", "Body is a bare int (value-type response)");
    });
    client.global.set("counterBefore", response.body);
%}

###

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# 2. Command — increment (IRequest<int> through closed CQRS + CounterTracingBehavior)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### [Feature: value-type command, closed open-generic behavior] Increment the counter
### Expect: 200 OK, body = previous value + 1.
### Observe stdout: SimpleLoggingBehavior timing for IncrementCounterCommand.
POST {{baseUrl}}/counter/increment

> {%
    client.test("Increment returns 200 with an int body", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "Expected 200 OK");
        client.assert(typeof response.body === "number", "Body is a bare int");
    });
    client.test("Increment returns previous value + 1", function () {
        const before = client.global.get("counterBefore");
        client.assert(response.body === before + 1, "Counter incremented by exactly 1");
    });
    client.global.set("counterAfter", response.body);
%}

###

### Increment again — confirm monotonic increase (state held in the singleton CounterStore)
POST {{baseUrl}}/counter/increment

> {%
    client.test("Second increment is greater than the first", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "Expected 200 OK");
        client.assert(response.body === client.global.get("counterAfter") + 1, "Incremented again by 1");
    });
%}

###

### Confirm GET reflects the latest value
GET {{baseUrl}}/counter
Accept: application/json

> {%
    client.test("Counter value persisted across requests", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "Expected 200 OK");
        client.assert(response.body >= client.global.get("counterBefore") + 2, "Counter advanced by the increments");
    });
%}

###

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# 3. CQRS boundary enforcement — nested request is rejected
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### [Feature: CQRS boundary enforcement] Illegal nested request
### The IllegalNestedCommand handler sends GetCounterQuery from WITHIN the handler, crossing the CQRS
### boundary. The generated closed CqrsBoundaryEnforcementBehavior throws CqrsBoundaryViolationException.
### Expect: failure (5xx). The counter is NOT mutated (handler short-circuits).
###
### Observe stdout: CqrsBoundaryViolationException — "CQRS boundary violation ... IllegalNestedCommand ... GetCounterQuery"
POST {{baseUrl}}/counter/illegal-nested

> {%
    client.test("Illegal nested request is rejected", function () {
        client.assert(response.status >= 400, "Expected a failure — CQRS boundary violation");
    });
%}

###

### Verify the counter was not changed by the rejected request
GET {{baseUrl}}/counter
Accept: application/json

> {%
    client.test("Counter unchanged after rejected nested request", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "Expected 200 OK");
        client.assert(response.body >= client.global.get("counterBefore") + 2, "Counter not decremented/reset by the rejected call");
    });
%}

###
